 Given the equation $\frac{1}{x} + \frac{1}{y} = \frac{1}{z}$, we can rearrange it to solve for $y$:
\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{x} + \frac{1}{y} &= \frac{1}{z} \\
\frac{1}{y} &= \frac{1}{z} - \frac{1}{x} \\
\frac{1}{y} &= \frac{x - z}{xz} \\
y &= \frac{xz}{x - z}
\end{align*}
Substituting $x = 25$ and $z = 24$ into the equation, we get:
\begin{align*}
y &= \frac{25 \cdot 24}{25 - 24} \\
y &= \frac{600}{1} \\
y &= 600
\end{align*> <answer> 600 </answer>

